# API contracts

## Package `@repo/api`

- Zod input schemas (`registerInputSchema`, `createGroupInputSchema`, …)
- Response schemas (`apiResponseSchema`, `authUserApiResponseSchema`, …)
- `tMessage` keys (`AUTH_T_MESSAGES`, `GROUP_T_MESSAGES`)
- DTO serializers (`serializeUser`, `serializeGroup`)
- `ApiError`, `isApiError`, `parseApiErrorPayload`, `createApiSuccessResponse`

Shared contracts only — no Express/Prisma logic here.

## Express backend (`backend/`)

- Parse input with `@repo/api` schemas
- Respond via `sendApiSuccess` / `sendApiError` from `backend/lib/api-response.ts`
- Auth logic and DB access live in routers, not in `@repo/api`
- Protected routes use `requireAuth`; optional-user routes use `optionalAuth`

## Next.js API routes (`app/api/`)

- Proxy to Express via `backendFetch` + `unwrapApiResponseData`
- Set httpOnly JWT cookie on login/register; body returns `{ user }` only (no token in JSON)
- Use `resolveRouteApiError` for catch blocks

## Client API (`src/lib/**/client-api.ts`)

- Thin fetch/tRPC wrappers used by forms
- Throw `ApiError` on failure; forms resolve messages via `useFormApiError` / `getSubmitError`
- `parseApiErrorPayload` must not treat `success: true` responses as errors

## parseApiErrorPayload rule

If `payload.success === true`, return `null`. Success responses also have a `message` field — do not treat that as an error.
